     "name_text": "apomorphine",
     "paragraphs": [
      {
       "span": {
        "end_line": 147,
        "start_line": 144
       },
       "text": "apomorphine, ondansetron. Mechanism: unspecified interaction mechanism. Contraindicated. Profound hypotension and loss of consciousness reported when 5HT3 antagonists are coadministered with apomorphine. Additionally, ondansetron may cause additive QT prolongation with apomorphine."
      }
     ],
     "span": {
      "end_line": 147,
      "start_line": 143
     }
    },
    {
     "header_line": 148,
     "name_text": "dronedarone",
     "paragraphs": [
      {
       "span": {
        "end_line": 150,
        "start_line": 149
       },
       "text": "dronedarone will increase the level or effect of ondansetron by affecting hepatic/intestinal enzyme CYP3A4 metabolism. Contraindicated."
      },
      {
       "span": {
        "end_line": 154,
        "start_line": 151
       },
       "text": "dronedarone and ondansetron both increase QTc interval. Contraindicated. Avoid with congenital long QT syndrome; ECG monitoring recommended with concomitant medications that prolong QT interval, electrolyte abnormalities, CHF, or bradyarrhythmias."
      }
     ],
     "span": {
      "end_line": 154,
      "start_line": 148
     }
    },
    {
     "header_line": 155,
     "name_text": "lefamulin",
     "paragraphs": [
      {
       "span": {
        "end_line": 158,
        "start_line": 156
       },
       "text": "lefamulin will increase the level or effect of ondansetron by affecting hepatic/intestinal enzyme CYP3A4 metabolism. Contraindicated. Lefamulin is contraindicated with CYP3A substrates know to prolong the QT interval."
      }
     ],
     "span": {
      "end_line": 158,
      "start_line": 155
     }
    },
    {
